From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: coop-fetch <coop-fetch@localhost>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Co-op pane body wrap: the dialogue box texts that skip the
 pane text wrap, to the module

Two more wrapped game functions in patch 0005's table
(nx2/coop_world_wraps.py WRAPS; their ids in host/hos_coop_pane_body.h),
for the module's play-test bridge (oot-remake-multiplayer's
docs/playtest.md "Text boxes"). They call the text box's set-string
themselves, so patch 0041's wrap (main+0x439520) never sees their texts:
- 26: main+0x76a460, a letter-animated pane's set-text (pane, text, length).
- 27: main+0x377a990, the set-text of each pane with a matching alias
  (pane, &{text, length}).
Phase 0 only reads. Nothing else changes: the wrap machinery, the checks
(build id, first words) and the hello's bits are 0005's.
---
 host/hos_coop_pane_body.h | 23 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 nx2/coop_world_wraps.py   |  6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 29 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 host/hos_coop_pane_body.h

diff --git a/host/hos_coop_pane_body.h b/host/hos_coop_pane_body.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0000000
--- /dev/null
+++ b/host/hos_coop_pane_body.h
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
+   Two more text pane setters for the play-test bridge (oot-remake-multiplayer, docs/playtest.md "Text boxes"): the
+   ones that skip the set-message call of patch 0041 (main+0x439520) and call the text box's set-string themselves.
+
+   Two wrapped game functions more in the one wrap table (patch 0005's nx2/coop_world_wraps.py WRAPS; the ids are in
+   the one wrap space of hos_coop_world.h). Patch 0042 adds their rows and this file (Hookshot's
+   host/hos_coop_pane_body.h is the same file). The module's hos_coop_wrap gets them; Hookshot announces them in
+   HOS_COOP_WORLD_HELLO's bits. The rows:
+     (26, 0x76a460, (0xd503237f, 0xa9bc7bfd, 0xa9015ff8, 0xa90257f6)),  # pacibsp; stp x29, x30; stp x24, x23; stp x22, x21
+     (27, 0x377a990, (0xd503237f, 0xa9bc7bfd, 0xf9000bf7, 0xa90257f6)),  # pacibsp; stp x29, x30; str x23; stp x22, x21
+   Phase 0 only reads (never skips). 26: x0 the pane (as 0041's), x1 the text, w2 its length (the low 16 bits); its
+   only caller is a letter-animated pane's set-text (a LetterAnimControl's vtable slot 7), so a dialogue box's
+   text. 27: x0 the pane, x1 a reference {+0 the text, +8 its length, +0x10 the attributes} as 0041's; called for
+   each text pane of a layout whose alias matches. Read from main only, not yet seen in a run. Plain C. */
+#ifndef HOS_COOP_PANE_BODY_H
+#define HOS_COOP_PANE_BODY_H
+
+/* main+0x76a460, a letter-animated text pane's set-text (pane, text, length). */
+#define HOS_COOP_WRAP_PANE_BODY 26u
+/* main+0x377a990, the set-text of each pane with a matching alias (pane, &{text, length}). */
+#define HOS_COOP_WRAP_PANE_ALIAS 27u
+
+#endif
diff --git a/nx2/coop_world_wraps.py b/nx2/coop_world_wraps.py
index 8cea7e3..0000000
--- a/nx2/coop_world_wraps.py
+++ b/nx2/coop_world_wraps.py
@@ -57,6 +57,12 @@ WRAPS = (
     # box keeps the pointer, so the module copies the text at the call, for the play-test bridge only
     # (oot-remake-multiplayer's docs/playtest.md "Text boxes"). Phase 0 reads only, never skips
     (25, 0x439520, (0xd503237f, 0xa9bd7bfd, 0xf9000bf5, 0xa9024ff4)),  # pacibsp; stp x29, x30; str x21; stp x20, x19
+    # HOS_COOP_WRAP_PANE_BODY (patch 0042): a letter-animated text pane's set-text (x0 the pane, x1 the text, w2
+    # its length): a dialogue box's text, which skips 0041's call. For the play-test bridge only, reads only
+    (26, 0x76a460, (0xd503237f, 0xa9bc7bfd, 0xa9015ff8, 0xa90257f6)),  # pacibsp; stp x29, x30; stp x24, x23; stp x22, x21
+    # HOS_COOP_WRAP_PANE_ALIAS (patch 0042): the set-text of each pane of a layout with a matching alias (x0 the
+    # pane, x1 a reference {+0 the text, +8 its length}). For the play-test bridge only, reads only
+    (27, 0x377a990, (0xd503237f, 0xa9bc7bfd, 0xf9000bf7, 0xa90257f6)),  # pacibsp; stp x29, x30; str x23; stp x22, x21
 )
 
 
